###  https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_74a75cf1_3418_4244_b43c_b5db94635d42
ns1:EMMO_74a75cf1_3418_4244_b43c_b5db94635d42 rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                              rdfs:subPropertyOf ns1:EMMO_814b6b76_e0ca_4953_a832_d1816fb695f1 ;
                                              rdf:type owl:AsymmetricProperty ,
                                                       owl:IrreflexiveProperty ;
                                              rdfs:domain ns1:EMMO_ee0466e4_780d_4236_8281_ace7ad3fc5d2 ;
                                              rdfs:range ns1:EMMO_9953c19f_ee33_4af8_be5e_dbf6d1e33581 ;
                                              rdfs:comment "The relation grouping all direct parthood relations used in the reductionistic perspective."@en ,
                                                           """Tiling parthood enables the establishment of hierarchy of granularities, starting with an entity and providing several tessellation levels according to specific criteria.
The criteria are implemented in specialised versions of the tiling parthood relation (e.g., metrological direct part, XML format direct part).
The tiles and the tessellated entity (tessellation) are causally self connected (i.e., items), coherently with the concept behind the definition of the reductionistic perspective.
The tiles of specific granularity level provide a covering for the whole and are mutually non-overlapping, as the label \"tile\" suggests."""@en ;
                                              rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/emmo/perspectives/reductionistic#> ;
                                              rdfs:label "hasTile"@en ;
                                              skos:altLabel "hasDirectPart"@en ;
                                              skos:prefLabel "hasTile"@en ;
                                              ns1:EMMO_31252f35_c767_4b97_a877_1235076c3e13 """Tiling parthood enables the establishment of hierarchy of granularities, starting with an entity and providing several tessellation levels according to specific criteria.
The criteria are implemented in specialised versions of the tiling parthood relation (e.g., metrological direct part, XML format direct part).
The tiles and the tessellated entity (tessellation) are causally self connected (i.e., items), coherently with the concept behind the definition of the reductionistic perspective.
The tiles of specific granularity level provide a covering for the whole and are mutually non-overlapping, as the label \"tile\" suggests."""@en ;
                                              ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 "The relation grouping all direct parthood relations used in the reductionistic perspective."@en ;
                                              ns1:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f "This relation is not antitransitive, to enable partitioning of a causal structure with more than one tiling scheme (e.g. time and space partitioning)."@en ,
                                                                                            "This relation is a simple collector of all relations inverse functional direct parthoods that can be defined in specialised theories using reductionism." .


