                                              rdfs:comment "A well defined physical entity, elementary or composite, usually treated as a singular unit, that is found at scales spanning from the elementary particles to molecules, as fundamental constituents of larger scale substances (as the etymology of \"particle\" suggests)."@en ,
                                                           "The union of hadron and lepton, or fermion and bosons."@en ;
                                              rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/emmo/reference/physicalistic#> ;
                                              rdfs:label "PhysicalParticle"@en ;
                                              skos:altLabel "Particle"@en ;
                                              skos:prefLabel "PhysicalParticle"@en ;
                                              ns1:EMMO_70fe84ff_99b6_4206_a9fc_9a8931836d84 "The union of hadron and lepton, or fermion and bosons."@en ;
                                              ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 "A well defined physical entity, elementary or composite, usually treated as a singular unit, that is found at scales spanning from the elementary particles to molecules, as fundamental constituents of larger scale substances (as the etymology of \"particle\" suggests)."@en ;
                                              ns1:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f "The scope of the physical particle definition goes from the elementary particles to molecules, as fundamental constituents of substances."@en .

