                           ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 """Specific heat capacity - The heat required to raise unit mass of a substance by unit temperature interval under specified conditions, such as constant pressure: usually measured in joules per kelvin per kilogram. Symbol c_p (for constant pressure) Also called specific heat.

