###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/characterisation-methodology/chameo#Profilometry
<https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/characterisation-methodology/chameo#Profilometry> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                                rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/characterisation-methodology/chameo#CharacterisationTechnique> ;
                                                                                rdfs:comment "Profilometry is a technique used to extract topographical data from a surface. This can be a single point, a line scan or even a full three dimensional scan. The purpose of profilometry is to get surface morphology, step heights and surface roughness."@en ;
