###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_0a6cf2fa_3466_4dd2_a7dd_e5a42cf9c386
:electrochemistry_0a6cf2fa_3466_4dd2_a7dd_e5a42cf9c386 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                       rdfs:subClassOf :electrochemistry_a2946006_513a_40cb_b4a8_710ea5401461 ;
                                                       rdfs:comment "the average characteristic size of the pores in a porous material, typically derived from a pore size distribution"@en ;
                                                       rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry/reference/electrochemistry-quantities#> ;
                                                       rdfs:label "MeanPoreSize"@en ;
                                                       skos:note "Mean pore size is a fundamental descriptor of porous materials that directly influences transport properties such as ionic conductivity, diffusion, and electrolyte accessibility in electrochemical systems. It is widely used in characterizing electrodes, separators, and catalysts. Including this term supports consistent semantic representation of structure–property relationships in electrochemistry."@en ;
                                                       skos:prefLabel "MeanPoreSize"@en ;
                                                       skos:scopeNote "Mean pore size is commonly obtained from techniques such as gas adsorption (e.g., BET/BJH analysis), mercury intrusion porosimetry, capilary flow porometery, or imaging methods. It complements related descriptors like pore size distribution, porosity, and specific surface area, which are already relevant in electrochemical material modeling."@en ;
                                                       ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 "the average characteristic size of the pores in a porous material, typically derived from a pore size distribution"@en ;
                                                       ns1:EMMO_fe015383_afb3_44a6_ae86_043628697aa2 "https://goldbook.iupac.org/terms/view/P04760" .


