                                                       ns1:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f "A typical construction is a tube of an inert material (e.g. agar agar) filled with a solution containing an electrolyte with approximately equal ion mobilities of the cation and the anion (e.g., KNO3, KCl), with the ends of the tube immersed in the electrolyte solution of the half cells."@en ;
