###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_7b3eb826_b968_493a_8396_cc3a5f09ecb3
:electrochemistry_7b3eb826_b968_493a_8396_cc3a5f09ecb3 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                       rdfs:subClassOf :electrochemistry_9bf40017_3f58_4030_ada7_cb37a3dfda2d ;
                                                       rdfs:comment "Internal resistance of an electrochemical cell determined from the voltage response to a direct-current pulse, calculated as ΔV/ΔI at a specified elapsed time after pulse onset."@en ;
                                                       rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry/reference/electrochemistry-quantities#> ;
                                                       rdfs:label "DCInternalResistance"@en ;
                                                       rdfs:seeAlso "ACInternalResistance" ;
                                                       skos:altLabel "DCIR"@en ;
                                                       skos:note "Encompasses contributions from ohmic resistance and from electrochemical kinetic processes — charge-transfer resistance and short-timescale diffusion — active within the measurement interval. Typically reported in milliohms (mΩ)"@en ;
                                                       skos:prefLabel "DCInternalResistance"@en ;
                                                       skos:scopeNote "Used to characterise power capability and resistive losses under pulsed discharge conditions; a standard output of the Hybrid Pulse Power Characterisation (HPPC) protocol."@en ;
                                                       ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 "Internal resistance of an electrochemical cell determined from the voltage response to a direct-current pulse, calculated as ΔV/ΔI at a specified elapsed time after pulse onset."@en ;
                                                       ns1:EMMO_b6730304_cabc_4104_b415_14218466445c "Values are not directly comparable between measurements made with different pulse durations or current magnitudes. Measurement conditions must be reported alongside the value."@en .


