###  https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry#electrochemistry_964cd426_f3cf_4a52_8c5d_0490cf48edb5
:electrochemistry_964cd426_f3cf_4a52_8c5d_0490cf48edb5 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                       rdfs:subClassOf :electrochemistry_9bf40017_3f58_4030_ada7_cb37a3dfda2d ;
                                                       rdfs:comment "The magnitude of the complex impedance of an electrochemical cell at a specified alternating-current frequency, typically 1 kHz."@en ;
                                                       rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/emmo/domain/electrochemistry/reference/electrochemistry-quantities#> ;
                                                       rdfs:label "ACInternalResistance"@en ;
                                                       skos:altLabel "ACIR"@en ;
                                                       skos:note "Determined by electrochemical impedance spectroscopy or by a single-frequency AC perturbation technique. Typically reported in milliohms (mΩ)."@en ;
                                                       skos:prefLabel "ACInternalResistance"@en ;
                                                       skos:scopeNote "At 1 kHz, reactive contributions from double-layer capacitance and Warburg diffusion are suppressed for typical battery geometries, making the result a practical approximation of ohmic resistance."@en ;
                                                       ns1:EMMO_4c8480cf_56de_41da_8699_f12a9033313a "The measurement frequency must be stated alongside the value. At frequencies above a few kilohertz, inductive reactance from cell tabs and interconnects can dominate the measured impedance."@en ;
                                                       ns1:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 "The magnitude of the complex impedance of an electrochemical cell at a specified alternating-current frequency, typically 1 kHz."@en ;
                                                       ns1:EMMO_b6730304_cabc_4104_b415_14218466445c "Characteristically lower than DCInternalResistance because electrochemical kinetic contributions are excluded at the measurement frequency. The two quantities must not be used interchangeably."@en .


